          <div class="comment__body break-text text-flow"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Hi, you should always have an independent test split, and do whatever you want with the other, e.g. Crossvalidation <a rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" href="https://scikit-learn.org/stable/_images/grid_search_cross_validation.png">visual sklearn reference</a></p>
<p lang="en" dir="ltr">Why are you losing lots of datapoint in the test split? the idea is that distributions match so you can use the p-value criteria for this.</p>
<p lang="en" dir="ltr">If you want to test lots of models try, optuna for finding the best hparams. No problem using the same metric, that's the one you care at the end.</p>
<p lang="en" dir="ltr">Depending on your domain I would ignore step 5, because you can test disfribution shifts, and even new models in time and be able to compare them.</p>
