<p lang="en" dir="ltr">If you take a look at papers or Kaggle, you will never find someone having both validation and test data locally. The test data usually is the real production data, or data you compare the models on. But you make decisions on your local cross validation to find a model that can generalize well on unseen test data (that is not in your current possession).</p>
